I didn't consider the implementation (I'm not going to try to
implement this).  I mostly wanted to examine the usefulness of the
scroll.

As far as I can tell, it's possible to have such a scroll without
changing the rules for what dungeon is generated.  Many things are
generated on the fly when you enter the level, but your actions don't
influence /what/ is created, so it could be precalculated without
changing the probabilities.

Asking for monsters ("where's the nearest gray dragon?") would be more
troublesome, since monster generation is based on what you do.  If
you're level 1, the correct answer might be "in the Castle, unless you
level up, which you probably will".

